ender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027.\n- Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2 2027.\n- Most of both plans is substations and transformers.\n- VLTX holdings won 60% of the last tender round (source: utility tender calendar).\n- VLTX utility order intake has risen every quarter, from C$610M in 2025Q4 to C$640M, C$655M and C$670M in 2026Q3. That is about 10% in three quarters, so growth is steady but decelerating.\n\n**Data centres (rising more slowly)**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027. That is slower than 2026, because power availability limits new sites.\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months.\n- A long queue means demand is backed up rather than weak. Equipment orders will likely be paced by grid capacity.\n\n**Risks**\n- Utility funding conditions are tightening. Bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, and two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Debt is still open but more expensive. That could delay or trim capex, though it is not a sign of falling demand. The financing question is covered by n3, and I haven't verified its conclusions.\n- Tender awards are lumpy, so quarterly order intake will be uneven.\n- I did not find VLTX's customer mix document, so I can't say how much of VLTX's orders depend on Pellham versus Norvane.","ttft_ms":2656,"type":"result","duration_ms":49803,"uuid":"61d8e5b2-c0a6-4aa6-b341-1c624146000a","ttft_stream_ms":1494,"time_to_request_ms":549,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":38,"system_prompt":64,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":81,"input_attachments":133,"input_hooks":12,"conversation_append":6,"transcript_persist":29,"tool_pool_refresh":5,"init_message":39,"init_frame_send":14,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":22,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":6,"request_announcements":28,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":15,"message_normalization":12,"c